  "sourceType": "PUBLIC_DOMAIN",
  "sourceNotes": "Ear-flap hats appear in Scandinavian and Andean folk knitting traditions. Weldon's Practical Knitter Series 10 describes ear-tab hats. Construction method used here is the standard incorporation at the cast-on.",
  "heroPrompt": "A finished ear-flap beanie in rust-red aran wool with two ear flaps hanging at the sides, showing the i-cord ties and the ribbed brim, lying on a wooden surface.",
